{
 "_doc": "Plomada 0.3: each AutoCAD block (AutoCAD MCP Pro catalogue item, DesignCenter block name or SITIO_ block) -> the 3D component that replaces its massing. Paths are relative to C:/mcp/biblioteca; skp null keeps the massing. fit: real = furniture at its own size (times scale), back on the block's back edge; footprint = furniture scaled to fit the block's w x d (for models drawn at the wrong scale); native = site object at its own size (times scale), centred on the block. rot (degrees CCW) turns a model whose front does not face -y (the SketchUp Front view) until it does. part = index of the one top-level group/component to use from a file that holds several objects. z lifts the model (mm). Instead of skp, src may name a .glb, .gltf, .dae or .stl that library_prepare (or the first build) imports and caches as a .skp (skp, default next to the source), normalised by src_scale (unit), front (-y, +x, +y, -x), up (+z, +y, -y, +x, -x, -z) and drop (node names to leave out).",
